utable split +and merge revisions with a typed structural payload. A split records the complete +reviewed support for one strictly ordered left visit and rebuilds with an +owner-boundary marker. A merge records two adjacent, strictly ordered single-visit +journeys and rebuilds them as one owner-visible successor. Both writes use the +existing immediate transaction, lifecycle/stale guards, idempotency key, and +redacted Atlas refresh. The owner correction screen previews both operations and +uses only opaque local visit and journey IDs. Save-time validation rejects weak, +same-day/unknown ordering, nonadjacent targets, missing support, and generated-ID +targets. Structural revisions are applied as grouping constraints rather than +being mapped to a generated journey target. + +Focused structural, correction UI, provider, migration, and repository suites +passed 6 suites / 60 tests; the complete mobile suite passed 28 suites / 218 +tests; mobile TypeScript and Expo lint passed; and root `npm run check` passed. +This is synthetic verification only. M4.1 remains in progress: merge currently +covers adjacent single-visit journeys, predecessor-wide claims still need durable +pending-scope records and owner resolution, the bounded uncertain-memory list and +competing-target view are incomplete, duplicate-family support identity is not +available from the adapter, destination removal and owner remap resolution remain +unimplemented, and physical iOS/Android validation has not been run. + +## M4.1 pending scope review (2026-10-14) + +Schema v24 adds durable `pending_scope_review` records. A structural split or +merge supersedes only predecessor-wide confirmation and owner title/date +revisions, publishes the structural successor in the same transaction, then +records each affected successor for owner scope review. A successor does not +show the predecessor claim as accepted. Saving a fresh scoped confirmation or +owner claim resolves that successor's pending-scope record. This is distinct +from `pending_remap`, which holds a later ambiguous automatic rebuild. + +The complete mobile suite passed 28 suites / 219 tests, and root `npm run +check` passed. Remaining M4.1 work includes destination removal, broad memory +review, duplicate-family identity, remap resolution, integration coverage of +titled predecessors and successor scope records, and device acceptance checks. + +## M4.1 destination removal (2026-10-14) + +Schema v25 adds a typed `remove-visit` correction revision. The owner selects +one opaque reviewed visit, previews the change, and saves an exact support-set +revision. Rebuild removes that visit only from the selected journey projection; +the visit, canonical evidence, place support, and country support remain in the +underlying reconstruction. The correction is stale/lifecycle guarded and uses +the existing atomic projection transaction. Full mobile verification passed 28 +suites / 220 tests, TypeScript, Expo lint, root `npm run check`, and diff +whitespace validation. Remaining M4.1 work is the durable remap-resolution UI +and candidate records, bounded uncertain-memory review with competing targets, +duplicate-family identity, acceptance-matrix integration coverage, and device +checks. + +## M4.1 pending-remap owner resolution (2026-10-14) + +An ambiguous correction remains withheld from the published projection and is now +visible only on a successor that overlaps its private reviewed support. The +journey review surface explains the bounded remap reason and offers two owner +paths: save a fresh scoped correction for the rebuilt journey, or preview and +discard the old withheld correction. Discarding supersedes only the pending +revision and candidate, then rebuilds and publishes the resulting complete graph +inside one SQLite transaction. It does not delete evidence, visits, places, +memories, or silently accept a successor. Candidate identifiers remain inside +the local repository and never enter the owner-readable detail contract. + +Focused UI, provider, reconstruction-repository, and migration suites passed 4 +suites / 47 tests, with mobile typecheck and Expo lint passing. This is +synthetic coverage. Remaining M4.1 work is bounded uncertain-memory review and +competing-target display, durable pending-remap handling for memory corrections, +duplicate-family identity when an adapter source is available, broader +acceptance-matrix integration coverage, and physical iOS/Android checks. + +## M4.1 uncertain-memory review (2026-10-14) + +The journey correction screen now opens a bounded, local page of photos that +lack visit support. Owners may search by observed date, page through at most 12 +rows at a time, see availability and coarse location-metadata state, and see how +many journey suggestions exist without exposing other journey identifiers. Each +row retains the existing preview-before-save assign, move, reject, and unassign +flow. A memory-only assignment remains separate from visit, place, country, and +owner-presence support. The database query and all opaque memory mappings remain +on device. + +Focused UI, provider, and reconstruction repository suites passed 3 suites / 36 +tests, with mobile typecheck and Expo lint passing. This is synthetic coverage. +Remaining M4.1 work includes durable pending-remap handling for memory +corrections, integration coverage for the full acceptance matrix, and physical +iOS/Android checks. Duplicate-family scoped correction remains unavailable until +the import adapter supplies a durable verified family identity and normalized +support tuple. + +## M4.1 code-level closure (2026-10-14) + +Schema v26 gives memory corrections their own durable pending-remap queue. An +automatic ambiguous memory remap is now retained for owner review and can be +discarded without affecting source evidence or unrelated corrections. The full +M4.1 implementation is ready for physical validation; use +`docs/development/m4-1-device-validation.md` for the private 